### Changes Made
1. **Added `PathSegment` & `parseSegments` Helper**:
   - Decomposes key tokens (e.g. `'users[0]'`) into structured segments:
     - The base property name (`'users'`, `isIndex: false`).
     - Any bracketed indices (`0`, `isIndex: true`).
2. **Updated `parseConfig` Construction**:
   - Uses `.flatMap(parseSegments)` on the parts returned by `splitKey`.
   - When creating intermediate container objects, inspects whether the next segment is an array index (`nextSeg.isIndex`). If so, initializes an Array (`[]`); otherwise, initializes an Object (`{}`).

```typescript
interface PathSegment {
  key: string | number;
  isIndex: boolean;
}

function parseSegments(part: string): PathSegment[] {
  const segments: PathSegment[] = [];
  const bracketRegex = /\[(\d+)\]/g;
  const firstBracket = part.indexOf('[');

  if (firstBracket === -1) {
    segments.push({ key: part, isIndex: false });
    return segments;
  }

  const prop = part.slice(0, firstBracket);
  if (prop.length > 0) {
    segments.push({ key: prop, isIndex: false });
  }

  let match: RegExpExecArray | null;
  while ((match = bracketRegex.exec(part)) !== null) {
    segments.push({ key: parseInt(match[1], 10), isIndex: true });
  }

  return segments;
}
```

